WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.000
Talent and power are hard to assess. Is a vampire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.280
really stronger than a werewolf? Are all&nbsp;
angels stronger than all demons? Here's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.280
a look at the most powerful villains on&nbsp;
Supernatural, from strong to strongest.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.560
No matter who Alastair is currently&nbsp;
possessing, he's always one of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:26.320
powerful demons. Hell's Grand Torturer answers&nbsp;
to few, save high-ranking demons like Lilith.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:31.920
He's tasked with torturing Dean for about four&nbsp;
months in Earth time in order to free Lucifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.720
from his God-built cage. Although&nbsp;
Dean is a human, and Alastair has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.640
home court advantage in Hell, the thought of&nbsp;
any entity having the ability to hold Dean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.920
down for that long further proves&nbsp;
that Alastair isn't a normal demon.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.400
His biggest claim to fame is playing&nbsp;
a role in triggering the apocalypse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.800
Even so, he's no match for Sam wielding&nbsp;
the full force of his psychic abilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.600
After pinning Alastair to the wall,&nbsp;
interrogating him about Lilith's plans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:10.640
and discovering his lack of knowledge, Sam&nbsp;
kills him. So goes one of Hell's absolute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.360
nastiest creatures — and one of&nbsp;
Supernatural's most memorable villains.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.920
Azazel isn't the most powerful villain of all&nbsp;
time, but the yellow-eyed demon is basically the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.400
reason John Winchester became a hunter, and&nbsp;
the reason he would go on to train his sons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.760
in the family business. Azazel murders Sam and&nbsp;
Dean's mother in Supernatural's pilot episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.960
launching the Winchesters' long, complex journeys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:40.640
as hunters of all that goes bump in the night.&nbsp;
He's basically the reason for the entire show.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.360
As a Prince of Hell, one of the first&nbsp;
generation of demons created by Lucifer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.960
he's already no average bad guy. Salt&nbsp;
and holy water have nothing on him — the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.880
Winchesters need a relic to take down Azazel.&nbsp;
Enter the Colt, a revolver that could kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.160
virtually anything. On the verge of elimination,&nbsp;
Dean shoots Azazel with the Colt and it works&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:08.160
like a charm. He isn't quite that easy to get&nbsp;
rid of, however: He continues to haunt the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:13.280
long past his demise. A Prince&nbsp;
of Hell casts a very long shadow.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:19.600
Metatron is an angel and the Scribe of God —&nbsp;
the only Scribe to ever have existed, in fact.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.360
Eons ago, he was responsible&nbsp;
for transcribing God's word,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:29.680
gaining universe-shaping information in the&nbsp;
process. He left Heaven to hide among humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.160
for fear of what the Archangels might do&nbsp;
to him in pursuit of that information.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:38.640
Metatron is the creator of the Angel&nbsp;
tablet, which grants immense power to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:44.480
those in contact with it — power he eventually&nbsp;
exploits to expel all angels from Heaven.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.080
While this makes Metatron unimaginably powerful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:53.840
his rule is short-lived, and he ends up locked in&nbsp;
Heaven's dungeon for his crimes. Even though he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.880
eventually imploded into nothingness by Amara,&nbsp;
he still remains an unforgettable character.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:07.840
The Alpha Vampire is the first vampire, and&nbsp;
therefore the paragon of all vampires. He knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:13.040
of the ancient leviathans and claims to remember&nbsp;
"the continental divide," which gives the audience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:20.000
an idea of how old and powerful he is. This is a&nbsp;
creature who has survived for millions of years as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:25.600
"the thing in the dark" — it would be an&nbsp;
understatement to say he's not to be trifled with.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:29.520
It can be argued that the Alpha&nbsp;
Vampire isn't truly villainous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.840
as he mostly just tries to live his&nbsp;
best life as a unique creature. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:40.480
at the same time, he did create vampires,&nbsp;
who have killed countless people. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:45.840
he falls to the legendary Colt, slayer&nbsp;
of entities otherwise invulnerable.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.440
Abaddon, a Knight of Hell, took down the&nbsp;
original Men of Letters single-handedly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:03.280
She's the worst kind of villain, at least from&nbsp;
the Winchesters' perspective: massively powerful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:10.160
and absolutely desperate for control. Trained by&nbsp;
the biblical Cain, Abaddon is an ancient threat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:15.680
well-accustomed to blood and mayhem.&nbsp;
There is no one she won't possess,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.120
slaughter, or maim in order to get what she wants.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:24.320
After time-traveling to the present day,&nbsp;
she decides to pursue her biggest plan yet:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:30.960
become the Queen of Hell. Like so many baddies,&nbsp;
she wants to rule the world through vast armies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:36.880
reserves of power, and iron law. Too bad&nbsp;
she comes across Sam and Dean Winchester.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:42.400
Dean, empowered by the Mark of Cain,&nbsp;
eventually kills Abaddon with the First Blade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:47.360
a relic once described as "the most&nbsp;
dangerous weapon on the planet."

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:53.760
Lilith is the first demon Lucifer ever created,&nbsp;
and the highest-ranking demon, second only to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.760 --> 00:05:00.240
Lucifer himself. She's also the final seal of&nbsp;
the 66 that, when broken, frees Lucifer from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:06.480
his cage. Even her death furthers a malicious&nbsp;
agenda. How's that for a commitment to evil?

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:14.160
Lilith's villainous resumé is long. She commands&nbsp;
a demon army, murders Dean with a hellhound, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:20.880
tortures countless humans. Although she arranges&nbsp;
for Sam to kill her, breaking the 66th seal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:27.600
she's eventually resurrected by God to retrieve&nbsp;
the Equalizer, a gun created by God that can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:35.520
kill anything. She destroys the gun and delivers&nbsp;
some truly terrible news: God's endgame is for Sam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:41.920
and Dean to kill each other. She's effortlessly&nbsp;
killed by the Archangel Michael not long after. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:47.920
short resurrection, but one that managed to shake&nbsp;
the foundations of the Supernatural universe.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.280
Rowena is arguably the most powerful&nbsp;
witch in the Supernatural universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:58.640
and really, not all that much of a bad&nbsp;
guy. She often helps Sam and Dean out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:04.560
sacrifices herself heroically, and even leaves&nbsp;
her magical possessions to Sam after her demise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:11.280
All this aside, however, she's season 10's&nbsp;
Big Bad : power-hungry, in possession of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:17.040
undeniably dark magic, and willing&nbsp;
to do anything to benefit herself.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:24.480
What makes Rowena so powerful? She's unstoppably&nbsp;
clever and thinks ten steps ahead of everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:29.120
else. For example, when Lucifer kills her,&nbsp;
she manages to come back to life thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:35.280
resurrection spells she'd prepared in advance.&nbsp;
A later death is orchestrated to drag the damned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:40.320
souls and demons, freed by God, back to Hell.&nbsp;
However, it's later revealed that she goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:45.680
on to become the Queen of Hell, so really,&nbsp;
she's not doing too badly in the afterlife.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:50.720
Crowley's resume is riddled with&nbsp;
good and evil, making him more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:56.720
of an antihero than a true out-and-out&nbsp;
bad guy. That said, Crowley is a demon:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:02.800
He's power-hungry, puts himself before all others,&nbsp;
and is generally predisposed towards nastiness.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:07.360
There are more powerful beings than&nbsp;
Crowley, but he's uniquely gifted.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:13.040
Son of Rowena, he uses his smarts to outwit&nbsp;
other beings, which allows him to survive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:18.960
and outlive more capable demons. And in the&nbsp;
real world, it also doesn't hurt that he's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:24.000
fan favorite — that's the sort of armor that&nbsp;
tends to keep a character healthy for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.600
no matter what kinds of shenanigans&nbsp;
they get themselves involved in.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:28.640
"I don't read Chinese"

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.280
"Talk about the dumbing down of America"

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:37.760
Though he's been everything from a human&nbsp;
to the King of Hell, Crowley is a demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:44.080
through and through. However, his final act is&nbsp;
heroic: He kills himself with an angelic blade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:50.400
to seal Lucifer in an alternate dimension.&nbsp;
Light or dark, Crowley is truly one of a kind.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:56.960
The Mother of All Monsters is named&nbsp;
Eve, and as her title suggests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:02.080
Eve created the very first versions&nbsp;
of each monster — the Alphas.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:08.080
Eve is older than angels and Hell&nbsp;
itself. She loves her children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:14.160
despite their monstrous natures, and while she&nbsp;
cannot claim the highest body count on the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:20.320
the amount of destruction and death her&nbsp;
children bring to the world is unfathomable.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:22.880
While Eve is only around for one season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:30.320
she isn't a pushover. There's only one viable way&nbsp;
to kill her: phoenix ash. Once the heroes find it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:36.080
Dean consumes the ash in a shot of liquor,&nbsp;
then goads Eve into biting him, killing her.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:40.640
Once upon a time, Dick Roman was&nbsp;
a billionaire businessman. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:45.680
he was murdered and replaced by the leader&nbsp;
of the leviathans, creatures so powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:50.240
God created Purgatory to lock them away&nbsp;
forever. When a billionaire is combined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:56.240
with God's first monsters, the result is one&nbsp;
of the most powerful beings on Supernatural.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:00.000
Leviathan Dick Roman isn't only one&nbsp;
of the oldest beings of the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.840
but he's also considered one of the most&nbsp;
powerful. Naturally, it takes a special weapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:11.280
the Bone of A Righteous Mortal Washed in the&nbsp;
Three Bloods of Fallen, to take him down for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:16.000
good. Without this weapon, the leviathans&nbsp;
likely would have taken over the world.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:21.760
Despite the leviathans' legendary brutality,&nbsp;
Leviathan Dick Roman only hangs around for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:27.440
a single season. He might be an ancient figure&nbsp;
of menace, but he goes up against Sam and Dean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:32.000
and eons-old baddies don't tend to fare&nbsp;
too well against the relentless brothers.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:37.600
Raphael is an archangel, one of the most&nbsp;
powerful creatures in the Supernatural universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:42.160
He can summon massive storms,&nbsp;
seems omniscient, and can blackout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:49.280
the entire Eastern Seaboard with a blink. He's&nbsp;
ancient, unknowable, and altogether scary.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:53.920
Although Raphael's time on Supernatural is&nbsp;
fairly short-lived, he's one of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:59.920
powerful beings on the show. Few things can&nbsp;
actually kill an archangel: Other archangels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:06.640
God, Amara, or a handful of ancient weapons.&nbsp;
He's about as untouchable as a creature can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:11.200
get — which makes it all the more impressive&nbsp;
that Castiel is able to take him down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:16.000
Even then, he can only do it when&nbsp;
supercharged by all the souls in Purgatory.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:22.640
Like his brothers Lucifer, Raphael, and Gabriel,&nbsp;
Michael is an archangel. However, the Michael of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:28.720
the alternate universe known as "Apocalypse World"&nbsp;
is easily one of the most powerful creations in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:35.360
the series and one of the toughest villains Sam&nbsp;
and Dean are ever forced to stop. In his world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.440
one torn apart by the absence of the&nbsp;
Winchester brothers, he's a conqueror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:45.360
of unimaginable power — he's often referred to&nbsp;
as the "Genghis Khan" of its ruined landscape.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:52.160
As the eldest son of God, alternate Michael is&nbsp;
arguably even more powerful than Lucifer himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:56.960
Some of the ingredients the Winchesters need&nbsp;
in the war against alternate Michael include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:05.920
hunters, Castiel, Rowena, Jack, Gabriel, Lucifer,&nbsp;
and countless others. The battle is arduous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:09.760
but Michael is eventually defeated by&nbsp;
Jack, who exploits Michael's hubris.

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:17.280
The original Death, in theory, is in the&nbsp;
top three strongest beings on Supernatural.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:24.000
Death has existed from the beginning of time&nbsp;
until his imminent demise. The original Death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:28.000
however, wasn't necessarily an&nbsp;
evil threat to the Winchesters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.080
The primordial entity was only&nbsp;
interested in keeping order.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:38.560
Eventually, Dean kills Death with his own scythe,&nbsp;
and Billie, a reaper killed by Castiel, is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:44.960
reincarnated and promoted as the new Death. Billie&nbsp;
assists the Winchesters in their endeavors and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:50.320
considered neutral for most of her time as Death.&nbsp;
She doesn't become a true villain until late in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:57.600
the series. As the new Death, she inherits powers&nbsp;
and is among the most potent entities, and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:04.080
the only being that can read God's book. But the&nbsp;
Shadow drags her to a place of nothingness known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:09.360
as the Empty, and her reign of terror ends. At&nbsp;
the height of her powers, though, Billie was one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:15.200
of the strongest villains on Supernatural — even&nbsp;
if she wasn't considered an antagonist for long.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:19.600
"This is the last time you'll&nbsp;
see me again. Until the end."

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:26.160
Lucifer is one of the most powerful villains&nbsp;
on Supernatural. A fallen archangel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:32.480
he's the original ruler of Hell and the&nbsp;
creator of demons; Lilith, the Princes of Hell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:37.520
the Knights of Hell, and all other manner&nbsp;
of dark creatures spring from his power.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:43.600
Despite his abilities and maliciousness, Lucifer&nbsp;
is actually a pretty likable character. Sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.560
the devil himself is oozing with darkness, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:51.120
this version of Lucifer is at&nbsp;
times laid-back and comical.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:55.040
Had it not been for the Winchesters,&nbsp;
Lucifer stood a very real chance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.040 --> 00:13:00.080
taking over the world. Eventually, he's put&nbsp;
down for good by alternate Michael and Dean.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:06.720
His soul then dwells in the Empty, a peaceful&nbsp;
void where divine creatures sleep forever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:11.760
Because living things don't stay dead&nbsp;
on Supernatural for long, Lucifer is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:18.080
resurrected by God — but then killed again, once&nbsp;
and for all, by Michael with an archangel blade.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:24.800
The Darkness, also known as Amara, has&nbsp;
existed since before the beginning of time;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:30.240
she's God's older sister. God had to create the&nbsp;
archangels to fight a war against her, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:34.080
they eventually won, and sealed&nbsp;
her away. She's the primordial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:38.880
origin point of all existence, the&nbsp;
"nothingness" that reigned before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:45.520
consciousness and creation. If either she or&nbsp;
God is destroyed, reality will cease to exist.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:51.600
Amara is presumably stronger than God, yet&nbsp;
God can, with the help of others, stop her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:58.240
As a pillar of reality itself, she's the most&nbsp;
powerful force the Winchesters have ever faced.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:02.080
Luckily for the Winchesters, The&nbsp;
Darkness leaves on her own terms.

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:08.160
But then, Amara completely rewrites history in the&nbsp;
final season, claiming that she and God were born&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:15.360
simultaneously. She allows God to absorb her, but&nbsp;
luckily, a juiced-up Jack absorbs God's powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:22.000
and becomes the new Almighty. Amara is also&nbsp;
absorbed by Jack, and they live in harmony.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:26.560
From an aspiring writer to&nbsp;
the creator of the universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:31.840
Chuck has a long and complicated history. Chuck&nbsp;
is seen as a good guy, or at least a mutual party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:37.280
to the Winchesters, for a good portion of the&nbsp;
series. It's not until the end of Supernatural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:42.480
when he's considered a full-on villain, and,&nbsp;
in fact, the Big Bad of the entire series.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:47.520
For a long time, Amara was the perceived&nbsp;
strongest being. But Chuck being revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:53.200
as the Big Bad of Supernatural counts for a&nbsp;
lot, as he's the final boss that stands in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:58.800
way of Dean and Sam's happiness. At the height&nbsp;
of his powers, Chuck absorbs Amara, making him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:05.120
an unstoppable force, and the most powerful&nbsp;
villain ever. But alas, it's short-lived:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:08.800
Jack strips Chuck of his powers, and the&nbsp;
creator of the universe is left to live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:14.560
out the rest of his days as a mere mortal. The&nbsp;
story, to Chuck's dismay, continues without him.

